# Shopping cart

A small catalog, a running cart of line items, a header badge counting them,
and a cart that survives a reload — its line items and its count alike.

## Note

The cart lives in one place. `## Store Cart persisted as "cart"` holds the line
items, `lines`, a `Seq of CartLine`; its two-parameter action `addLine` is called
as `Call Cart's addLine with name and price.`, and gives each new line the id one
past the highest in the cart (`nextIdFor`). The header's `CartBadge` and the side
panel both read `Cart's lines`, so the count, the list and the total never
disagree. A persisted store keeps its fields in local storage through the JSON
codec derived from their types, so a reload brings back the same cart.

`CartPanel` draws the cart and takes what "remove" means as a prop,
`remove: fn(Int) -> Unit`: the page hands it `removeLine`, and each row's button
calls `remove(line's id)` — `docs/frontend.md`'s "Passing actions down".

## A CartLine has:
    an id, which is Int.
    a name, which is Text.
    a price, which is Int.

## To nextIdFor (lines: Seq of CartLine) -> Int:
    Let mutable highest be 0.
    Repeat for line in lines:
        If line's id is greater than highest:
            Set highest to line's id.
    Return highest + 1.

## To sumPrices (lines: Seq of CartLine) -> Int:
    Let mutable total be 0.
    Repeat for t in lines:
        Set total to total + t's price.
    Return total.

## To formatCents (cents: Int) -> Text:
    Let dollars be cents / 100.
    Let remainder be cents - dollars * 100.
    If remainder is less than 10:
        Return "${dollars}.0{remainder}".
    Return "${dollars}.{remainder}".

## Store Cart persisted as "cart"

State:
    Let lines be a new Seq of CartLine.

Actions:
    To addLine (name: Text) and (price: Int):
        Push (a new CartLine with id nextIdFor(lines) and name name and price price) to lines.

    To removeLine (id: Int):
        Remove every line from lines where line's id is equal to id.

## Component CartBadge

Use Cart.

View:
    <span id="badge">{length of Cart's lines} in cart</span>

## Component CartPanel (remove: fn(Int) -> Unit)

Use Cart.

View:
    <aside>
      <h2>Cart</h2>
      <ul class="panel">
        {for each line in Cart's lines, keyed by line's id:}
          <li id="line-{line's id}"><span class="name">{line's name} — {formatCents(line's price)}</span> <button id="remove-{line's id}" on-click={remove(line's id)}>remove</button></li>
        {else:}
          <li class="empty">Your cart is empty.</li>
        {end}
      </ul>
      <p id="total">Total: {formatCents(sumPrices(Cart's lines))}</p>
    </aside>

## Page /

Use Cart.

Actions:
    To addProduct (name: Text) and (price: Int):
        Call Cart's addLine with name and price.

    To removeLine (id: Int):
        Call Cart's removeLine with id.

View:
    <header>
      <h1>The Corner Store</h1>
      <CartBadge/>
    </header>
    <main class="catalog">
      <ul>
        <li>Tea — {formatCents(300)} <button id="add-tea" on-click={addProduct("Tea", 300)}>add</button></li>
        <li>Coffee — {formatCents(450)} <button id="add-coffee" on-click={addProduct("Coffee", 450)}>add</button></li>
        <li>Muffin — {formatCents(250)} <button id="add-muffin" on-click={addProduct("Muffin", 250)}>add</button></li>
      </ul>
    </main>
    <CartPanel remove={removeLine}/>

Style:
    header { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; padding: 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
    main.catalog ul, .panel { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
    .panel .empty { color: var(--muted); }

## Test: the cart starts empty

Expect that the text of "#badge" is equal to "0 in cart".
Expect that the text of ".empty" is equal to "Your cart is empty.".
Expect that the text of "#total" is equal to "Total: $0.00".

## Test: adding a product lists it, counts it and totals it

Click "#add-tea".
Expect that the text of "#line-1 .name" is equal to "Tea — $3.00".
Expect that the text of "#badge" is equal to "1 in cart".
Expect that the text of "#total" is equal to "Total: $3.00".
Expect that the count of ".empty" is equal to 0.
Click "#add-coffee".
Click "#add-tea".
Expect that the count of ".panel li" is equal to 3.
Expect that the text of "#line-2 .name" is equal to "Coffee — $4.50".
Expect that the text of "#line-3 .name" is equal to "Tea — $3.00".
Expect that the text of "#badge" is equal to "3 in cart".
Expect that the text of "#total" is equal to "Total: $10.50".

## Test: a row's remove button drops exactly that line

Click "#add-tea".
Click "#add-coffee".
Click "#remove-1".
Expect that the count of ".panel li" is equal to 1.
Expect that the text of "#line-2 .name" is equal to "Coffee — $4.50".
Expect that the text of "#badge" is equal to "1 in cart".
Expect that the text of "#total" is equal to "Total: $4.50".
Click "#remove-2".
Expect that the text of ".empty" is equal to "Your cart is empty.".
Expect that the text of "#badge" is equal to "0 in cart".
Expect that the text of "#total" is equal to "Total: $0.00".

## Test: the cart and its count survive a reload

Click "#add-tea".
Click "#add-coffee".
Click "#remove-1".
Click "#add-muffin".
Reload the page.
Expect that the text of "#badge" is equal to "2 in cart".
Expect that the count of ".panel li" is equal to 2.
Expect that the text of "#line-2 .name" is equal to "Coffee — $4.50".
Expect that the text of "#line-3 .name" is equal to "Muffin — $2.50".
Expect that the text of "#total" is equal to "Total: $7.00".

## Test: a line added after a reload takes the next free id

Click "#add-tea".
Click "#add-coffee".
Reload the page.
Click "#add-muffin".
Expect that the count of ".panel li" is equal to 3.
Expect that the text of "#line-3 .name" is equal to "Muffin — $2.50".
Expect that the text of "#badge" is equal to "3 in cart".
